{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/b1-explainer-about-recent-ai-models-mythos-5-1-gpt-astra-and-j-space-and-research-systems/audio/main-56d2f9291422.mp3","durationSec":272.448,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":5.14,"text":"We can use three questions: What is the source, what changed, and what was the result?"},{"start":5.98,"end":8.42,"text":"The source may be a company or a research team."},{"start":9.26,"end":14,"text":"The change may be a stronger model, different safety rules, or a new research tool."},{"start":14.68,"end":17.8,"text":"The result affects how people can use or study the system."},{"start":18.88,"end":24.22,"text":"In July 2026, Anthropic published research about J-space inside Claude models."},{"start":24.76,"end":29.98,"text":"Around 1 September, it introduced Mythos 5.1 for trusted specialist work."},{"start":30.76,"end":35.88,"text":"Around 3 September, OpenAI released GPT-6 Astra to a limited set of customers."},{"start":36.72,"end":39.98,"text":"These developments are connected, but they are not the same kind of thing."},{"start":40.58,"end":41.64,"text":"Two are model releases."},{"start":41.64,"end":45.08,"text":"J-space is a research finding, not a product."},{"start":45.78,"end":51.98,"text":"Anthropic introduced two versions of the same underlying model: Fable 5.1 and Mythos 5.1."},{"start":52.2,"end":55.2,"text":"They have the same learned core, but different safeguards."},{"start":56.12,"end":63.4,"text":"Fable 5.1 became generally available for coding, knowledge work, and long problem-solving."},{"start":63.4,"end":69.1,"text":"It can help find weaknesses in software code, but it blocks help with developing ways to attack those weaknesses."},{"start":70.4,"end":76.02,"text":"Mythos 5.1 has more permissive safeguards for approved cyber and life-science research."},{"start":76.7,"end":80.08,"text":"For this reason, it is invite-only."},{"start":80.08,"end":87.4,"text":"Vetted people and groups can receive access through the Cyber Verification Program or the Life Sciences Verification Program."},{"start":88.56,"end":98.48,"text":"Mythos 5.1 also powers Claude Security, a tool that scans collections of code, finds possible security problems, and suggests repairs for a person to review."},{"start":99.46,"end":102.64,"text":"Here, stronger access depends on trust and purpose."},{"start":103.26,"end":109.26,"text":"OpenAI released GPT-6 Astra to a limited group around 3 September 2026."},{"start":109.96,"end":117.18,"text":"The model can control computer systems and complete tasks for users, such as filling spreadsheets or building websites."},{"start":118.26,"end":124.1,"text":"OpenAI described it as a strong step for computer use, coding, science, and professional work."},{"start":124.66,"end":127.9,"text":"Its cyber ability also created serious risk."},{"start":128.74,"end":137.88,"text":"Under OpenAI’s Preparedness Framework, GPT-6 Astra was the first OpenAI model to reach the Critical cybersecurity capability level."},{"start":138.5,"end":150.16,"text":"With suitable tools and access, it can find previously unknown security weaknesses and develop ways to use them against many well-protected systems without a person directing every step."},{"start":150.92,"end":154.48,"text":"OpenAI therefore added stronger safeguards and monitoring."},{"start":154.48,"end":163.02,"text":"Access began with cyber defenders in the Daybreak program, while wider ChatGPT and API access was planned for the following days."},{"start":163.02,"end":166.58,"text":"J-space is not another chatbot."},{"start":167.16,"end":173.58,"text":"It is a small set of internal neural patterns that researchers found inside language models such as Claude."},{"start":173.58,"end":177.74,"text":"They used the J-lens, short for Jacobian lens, to find these patterns."},{"start":178.54,"end":184.26,"text":"Each pattern connects to a word that is on the model’s “mind,” even when the model does not write that word."},{"start":185.22,"end":191.36,"text":"Researchers call this a global workspace because important concepts appear in a shared internal channel."},{"start":191.88,"end":197.24,"text":"It works silently and is different from a written chain of thought, which is an explanation shown in words."},{"start":198.02,"end":202.6,"text":"By studying J-space, researchers can sometimes see hidden concepts."},{"start":203.24,"end":208.26,"text":"This may help them notice when a model is going off track or possibly cheating on a safety test."},{"start":208.66,"end":214.08,"text":"The J-lens does not open every thought, but it offers a new way to inspect some internal activity."},{"start":215.02,"end":218.5,"text":"These examples show that “better” can mean several things."},{"start":219.24,"end":223.84,"text":"A model may become more capable, but people also need ways to manage its risks."},{"start":224.84,"end":231.92,"text":"Anthropic used different safeguards and trusted-access programs for Fable 5.1 and Mythos 5.1."},{"start":232.44,"end":239.38,"text":"OpenAI used its Preparedness Framework, monitoring, and staged access for GPT-6 Astra."},{"start":239.8,"end":244.34,"text":"These systems control what a model may do and who can use its strongest abilities."},{"start":244.34,"end":249.08,"text":"J-space supports a different goal: understanding internal activity."},{"start":249.82,"end":254.76,"text":"It may help researchers see silent concepts and detect troubling behavior during a test."},{"start":255.46,"end":256.96,"text":"So we can reuse our lens."},{"start":257.76,"end":260.2,"text":"The source is a company or research team."},{"start":260.82,"end":265.2,"text":"The change is a model, safeguard, access program, or inspection tool."},{"start":265.82,"end":271.88,"text":"The result may be stronger performance, safer access, or a clearer view of what is happening inside."}],"words":[{"text":"We","start":0,"end":0.16},{"text":"can","start":0.16,"end":0.3},{"text":"use","s